In-house core stage 3d (issue #18): Linux/OpenSBI boot attempt
Outcome: BLOCKED on the A extension (stage 4), as expected —
recorded here so the stage-3 gate is an attempt with evidence,
not a skip.

What was tried
--------------
1. Host toolchain build of OpenSBI (generic platform):
     make PLATFORM=generic CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-elf-
   -> "Your linker does not support creating PIEs, opensbi
      requires this" (bare-metal riscv64-elf-ld on this host;
      no riscv64-linux-gnu toolchain installed).

2. Docker build (ubuntu:24.04 + gcc-riscv64-linux-gnu):
     make PLATFORM=generic CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-linux-gnu-
   -> builds cleanly (fw_jump/fw_dynamic/fw_payload .elf).
   But the result targets RV64GC: ELF flags "RVC,
   soft-float ABI", 36,302 of 61,498 instructions are
   2-byte compressed (our stage-3 core is IALIGN=32;
   C arrives at stage 5), and it contains lr/sc/amo
   instructions (A extension, stage 4).

3. RV64IM build override, matching this core:
     make PLATFORM=generic CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-linux-gnu- \
       PLATFORM_RISCV_ISA=rv64im_zicsr_zifencei \
       PLATFORM_RISCV_ABI=lp64
   -> lib/sbi/riscv_locks.c:68:2: error:
      #error "need A or Zaamo or Zalrsc"
   OpenSBI has no supported configuration without atomics,
   and Linux proper requires A (and in practice C) too.

Prerequisites for a real boot, in stage order
---------------------------------------------
- Stage 4: A (lr/sc + AMOs) — unblocks OpenSBI; F/D as
  planned for kernel/userland ABI.
- Stage 5: C (IALIGN=16) — OpenSBI/Linux can be built
  without it, but stock binaries assume it.
- Harness devices (small, do with stage 4): CLINT
  (mtime/mtimecmp -> irq_m_timer_i, MSIP), an 8250 UART
  (THR -> stdout), and a DTB describing them; the core
  side already has the interrupt pins, PMP, Sv39 and
  delegation OpenSBI needs. Performance work (iterative
  divider, caches) determines how far a kernel boot gets
  in reasonable wall-clock on Verilator.
